    "lawCode": "Amd §13, Chap 405 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5229\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 405 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing\nthe lease of lands located at the state university of New York at\nPurchase, in relation to the permitted use of proceeds from the lease of\nsuch lands\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis bill permits the board of trustees of Purchase college to use twen-\nty-five per cent of the proceeds from the lease of land located at the\nstate university of New York at Purchase, which is currently allocated\nfor \"additional\" full-time faculty, to be used to support current full-\ntime faculty as well.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 13 of chapter 405 of authorizing the lease of\nlands located at the Purchase to allow twenty-five per cent of the used\nto support current as well as additional\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.  the laws of 2011 relating to state\nuniversity of New York at proceeds from such lease to be full-time\nfaculty positions.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 405 of the Laws of 2011 authorized the lease of lands of the\nstate university of New York at Purchase to the Purchase college\nadvancement corporation, to be used as the site of a senior living\ncommunity. This bill would slightly expand the permitted uses of the\nfunds generated from that lease.\n\nUnder existing law, the board of trustees of Purchase college is\ndirected to allocate seventy-five per cent of the lease proceeds to\nstudent financial aid, and twenty-five per cent to \"additional full-time\nfaculty positions.\" This bill would permit use of the twenty-five\npercent for current as well as additional full-time faculty.\n\nThe change reflects the nature of higher education at the current moment\nas compared to 2011 when the statute was enacted. Given current enroll-\nment trends and the need to retain current faculty to best serve\nstudents, and a somewhat less urgent need for new faculty at this time,\nthis bill would facilitate and support the college's efforts to meet the\nneeds of students and to retain qualified faculty to staff the college's\nprograms.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
